<figure class="fig" aria-label="LangSmith bundles sandboxes, an auth proxy and tracing with the platform. ZenML gives you isolated steps, a sandbox stack component with Docker, Kubernetes and Modal flavors, and secrets scoped to the step, while tool permissions stay with the harness.">
  <div class="panel panel--competitor">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <span class="panel-label">LangSmith · packaged security</span>
      <span class="panel-sub">Isolation bundled with the runtime</span>
    </div>

    <div class="block">
      <span class="block-title">LangSmith Sandboxes</span>
      <span class="block-sub">ephemeral, locked-down environments</span>
    </div>
    <div class="block">
      <span class="block-title">Auth proxy</span>
      <span class="block-sub">secrets never enter the sandbox</span>
    </div>
    <div class="block">
      <span class="block-title">OpenTelemetry tracing</span>
      <span class="block-sub">native to the platform</span>
    </div>

    <div class="foot">Usable isolation story out of the box.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel panel--zenml">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <span class="panel-label panel-label--accent">ZenML · configurable boundary</span>
      <span class="panel-sub">Isolation is a stack component</span>
    </div>

    <div class="api">
      <span class="api-call"><span class="fn">@step</span>(runtime=<span class="str">"isolated"</span>)</span>
      <span class="api-sub">separate pod / job on your stack</span>
    </div>

    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row">
        <span class="rkey">Sandbox</span>
        <span class="rval">Docker · Kubernetes · Modal</span>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <span class="rkey">Secrets</span>
        <span class="rval">zenml secret create, secrets= on the step</span>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <span class="rkey">Tool permissions</span>
        <span class="rval">stay with the harness</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="foot foot--accent">Your sandbox, your secrets, your cloud. Tool policy is the harness's job.</div>
  </div>
</figure>

